Installation only proceeds when the host UI *accepts* the elicitation.

=== 3. `codex exec` auto-cancels every elicitation
=== codex-rs/exec/src/lib.rs

  1661:    let handle_result = match request {
  1662:        ServerRequest::McpServerElicitationRequest { request_id, .. } => {
  1663:            // Exec auto-cancels elicitation instead of surfacing it
  1664:            // interactively. Preserve that behavior for attached subagent
  1665:            // threads too so we do not turn a cancel into a decline/error.
  1666:            match canceled_mcp_server_elicitation_response() {

Therefore `user_confirmed` is always false under `codex exec`, and step 2 can
never complete an install — regardless of the allowlist. This is the decisive
fact: the rejection observed in production is not the only barrier, it is the
first of two.

