=== codex-rs/core/src/context/recommended_plugins_instructions.rs

     6:const MAX_RECOMMENDED_PLUGINS: usize = 50;
    21:                .take(MAX_RECOMMENDED_PLUGINS)
    38:        ("<recommended_plugins>", "</recommended_plugins>")

Entries come from `GET {chatgpt_base_url}/ps/plugins/suggested?scope=GLOBAL`
for the authenticated account. There is no local configuration key that adds
an entry, so a repository cannot make its mandatory plugin installable this
way.

=== 5. The two marketplace spellings are genuinely distinct upstream
=== codex-rs/core-plugins/src/lib.rs

    26:pub const OPENAI_CURATED_MARKETPLACE_NAME: &str = "openai-curated";
    27:pub const OPENAI_API_CURATED_MARKETPLACE_NAME: &str = "openai-api-curated";
    32:pub fn is_openai_curated_marketplace_name(marketplace_name: &str) -> bool {
    33:    marketplace_name == OPENAI_CURATED_MARKETPLACE_NAME
    34:        || marketplace_name == OPENAI_API_CURATED_MARKETPLACE_NAME
    35:}

=== codex-rs/core-plugins/src/remote.rs

    69:pub const REMOTE_GLOBAL_MARKETPLACE_NAME: &str = "openai-curated-remote";
    70:pub const REMOTE_CREATED_BY_ME_MARKETPLACE_NAME: &str = "created-by-me-remote";
    71:pub const REMOTE_WORKSPACE_MARKETPLACE_NAME: &str = "workspace-directory";

`openai-curated` is the local marketplace `codex plugin add` installs from.
`openai-curated-remote` is the synthesized namespace the recommended-plugin
list is built under (`remote.rs:888-891` constructs every recommended
`PluginId` with `REMOTE_GLOBAL_MARKETPLACE_NAME`), which is why the model asked
for `superpowers@openai-curated-remote` and why Hive Mind must rewrite that
selector to `superpowers@openai-curated` before calling `codex plugin add`.

